{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986226-is-cruac-really-this-bad","id":986226,"title":"Is Cruac really this bad?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-12T11:05:01-07:00","id":986226,"title":"Is Cruac really this bad?","content":"I'm just reading through VtR 2nd edition, and came on Cruac.<br /> <br /> Considering those rituals take forever to accomplish, their results seem... underwhelming. At least the few low level rituals.<br /> <br /> In the 1st edition or VtM where 1st level Disciplines are also pretty crap I could accept that, but in VtR2 the 1st dot feels often more powerful than 1-3 together previously, so these rituals just seem bad to me.<br /> <br /> Has there been some supplements that make them better?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:12:21-07:00","id":986232,"title":"","content":"Secrets of the Covenants, which is in proofing right now, will have new Cr\u00faac. And if you have a look at Blood Sorcery: Sacraments and Blasphemies, the systems and spells there are compatible with the new system; the book was used to convert the spells in VtR2nd.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:23:23-07:00","id":986240,"title":"","content":"I thought the Blood Sorcery book came out before VtR2 ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:30:00-07:00","id":986247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986226-is-cruac-really-this-bad?p=986240#post986240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Blood Sorcery book came out before VtR2 ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It did, but the 2e Blood Sorcery system was based in the Sacriments and Blasphemies system. The problem is, the S&amp;B Blood Sorcery system was broken as hell with casting times in a matter of turns, so 2e &quot;fixed&quot; it by increasing the interval to 30 minutes. Which works great if you're using creative casting from S&amp;B, but the sample rituals they put in 2e were the same as the ones from the 1e core book, which were designed before S&amp;B, and are pretty useless without a 1-turn casting interval.<br /> <br /> So, when Secrets of the Covenants comes out, it will include rituals that are actually worthwhile for the time it takes to cast them. In the mean time, you're probably better off using S&amp;B, with 2e's changes to the casting time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:31:14-07:00","id":986250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986226-is-cruac-really-this-bad?p=986240#post986240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the Blood Sorcery book came out before VtR2 ?</div> </div> </div> </div>It did. You can see it mentioned in the sidebar on p151.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:47:59-07:00","id":986266,"title":"","content":"Ok, I had a look at Blood Sorcery now, but only skimmed it real quick. <br /> <br /> Let me know if I understand it somewhat correctly, or if I'm totally off.<br /> <br /> There are now 5 &quot;themes&quot;: Creation, Destruction, Divination, Protection and Transmutation<br /> <br /> I have to buy dots in these Themes in addition to my dots in Cruac. How expensive are they? I assume my dots in the Themes are limited to my Cruac dots?<br /> <br /> Then I can learn the rituals, assuming I have enough dots in the Themes? &quot;Harvest of Slaves&quot; is Transmutation 1, so I need 1 dot in that, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Duration, Range, Number of Targets etc, are all determined by what I pick on 17/18.<br /> So if I wanted to cast my &quot;Harvest of Slaves&quot; Ritual with a 1 yard radius (+0), lasts till sunrise (+3), affects one target (+0), Potency 2 (+1), over one mile (+2), up to 20 size (+0) would result in a target number of 6.<br /> <br /> So now I'd roll Manipulation + Survival + Transmutation (because it's a Transmutation Cruac ritual, or is it the Man + Occult + Theme roll?), with a 30 minute duration per roll, and try to get 6 hits?<br /> <br /> I've no idea if those options make any sense for that particual ritual, just wanting to know if I sort of understand how it works.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T11:49:31-07:00","id":986270,"title":"","content":"I think each dot of Cruac you get a free dot in a theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T12:31:46-07:00","id":986303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986226-is-cruac-really-this-bad#post986226\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm just reading through VtR 2nd edition, and came on Cruac.<br /> <br /> Considering those rituals take forever to accomplish, their results seem... underwhelming. At least the few low level rituals.<br /> <br /> In the 1st edition or VtM where 1st level Disciplines are also pretty crap I could accept that, but in VtR2 the 1st dot feels often more powerful than 1-3 together previously, so these rituals just seem bad to me.<br /> <br /> Has there been some supplements that make them better?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Quantity over quality? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T12:44:33-07:00","id":986313,"title":"","content":"Well there are only 2 per level in the VtR book, so it's not even quantity...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T13:54:19-07:00","id":986363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986226-is-cruac-really-this-bad?p=986266#post986266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I had a look at Blood Sorcery now, but only skimmed it real quick. <br /> <br /> Let me know if I understand it somewhat correctly, or if I'm totally off.<br /> <br /> There are now 5 &amp;quot;themes&amp;quot;: Creation, Destruction, Divination, Protection and Transmutation<br /> <br /> I have to buy dots in these Themes in addition to my dots in Cruac. How expensive are they? I assume my dots in the Themes are limited to my Cruac dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>When you buy your first dot of Cruac, you get two free dots of Themes divided as you choose between Creation and Protection, and a third free dot of any other Theme. After that, each time you gain a dot in Cruac, you get a free dot in any Theme you already have at least one dot in. You can also buy Theme dots for Experiences. In 1e, Theme dots cost [5x new dot] experience points, which equates to 3 Experiences per dot in 2e. You cannot have more dots in any one Theme than you have dots in Cruac.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986226-is-cruac-really-this-bad?p=986266#post986266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then I can learn the rituals, assuming I have enough dots in the Themes? &amp;quot;Harvest of Slaves&amp;quot; is Transmutation 1, so I need 1 dot in that, I suppose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every time you gain a dot in a Theme, you gain a free Ritual that uses the same Theme, at your new dot rating or lower. You can also buy new rituals for Experiences. But, you can also use your Themes to improvise rituals, just like Mages can use their Arcana to improvise spells. So, yes, since Harvest of Slaves is a Transmutation 1 Ritual, you need at least 1 dot of Transmutation to reproduce it with an improvised ritual, and if you want to cast it as a learned ritual, need to either buy it with Experiences or get it when you increase your Transmutation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986226-is-cruac-really-this-bad?p=986266#post986266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Duration, Range, Number of Targets etc, are all determined by what I pick on 17/18.<br /> So if I wanted to cast my &amp;quot;Harvest of Slaves&amp;quot; Ritual with a 1 yard radius (+0), lasts till sunrise (+3), affects one target (+0), Potency 2 (+1), over one mile (+2), up to 20 size (+0) would result in a target number of 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. Factors are all determined by what you pick if you improvise the ritual. If you perform it as a learned ritual, those factors are fixed, and are determined at the time that you learn the ritual. The example rituals in the VtR 2e core book are all built as learned rituals using this system, for example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986226-is-cruac-really-this-bad?p=986266#post986266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So now I'd roll Manipulation + Survival + Transmutation (because it's a Transmutation Cruac ritual, or is it the Man + Occult + Theme roll?), with a 30 minute duration per roll, and try to get 6 hits?</div> </div> </div> </div>By the book, you roll Manipulation + Survival + Transmutation if you're performing it as a learned ritual, or Manipulation + Occult + Transmutation if you are performing it as an improvised ritual. Personally, I house rule it to use Manipulation + Survival + Transmutation for improvised rituals and Manipulation + Occult + Cruac for learned rituals. This is a pretty common house rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986226-is-cruac-really-this-bad?p=986266#post986266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've no idea if those options make any sense for that particual ritual, just wanting to know if I sort of understand how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got the right idea for the most part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-12T15:32:41-07:00","id":986436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986226-is-cruac-really-this-bad?p=986363#post986363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes and no. Factors are all determined by what you pick if you improvise the ritual. If you perform it as a learned ritual, those factors are fixed, and are determined at the time that you learn the ritual. The example rituals in the VtR 2e core book are all built as learned rituals using this system, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I hadn't found yet that you need to set the stuff on learned ritual when you learn it. <br /> Wouldn't that make improvised rituals way more flexible? You can spend extra successes on learned rituals, to increase some effects, which you can't for improvised ones, but you can just set the threshold higher to begin with. Also you can't make it weaker with learned ones, with improvised you could.<br /> Also Improvised ones don't cost XP to learn.<br /> <br /> To be honest the difference between Learned and Improvised rituals is not very clear, even though there is a separate section titled exactly that.<br /> It just mentions that &quot;Improvised rituals are slower and more difficult to perform than those the caster has memorized and made part of herself.&quot; But I couldn't find anywhere how much longer and how much more difficult.<br /> <br /> Can I still improvise a Ritual even though I know it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986226-is-cruac-really-this-bad?p=986363#post986363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the book, you roll Manipulation + Survival + Transmutation if you're performing it as a learned ritual, or Manipulation + Occult + Transmutation if you are performing it as an improvised ritual. Personally, I house rule it to use Manipulation + Survival + Transmutation for improvised rituals and Manipulation + Occult + Cruac for learned rituals. This is a pretty common house rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it seems backwards to me too.<br /> <br /> If I improvise I just learn Manipulation + Occult and max those and then I'm good. For learned I need Attributes and Skills all over the place. So making learned rituals use the same skill all the time, and if you improvise it, you have to use specialized ones, makes more sense really.<br /> <br /> By strict RAW Improvised seems better than Learned.<br /> <br /> So, now I just have to convince my ST to allow all this. I guess the fact the book is referenced in the sidebar might help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T02:05:12-07:00","id":986640,"title":"","content":"Edit: Never mind, misread a thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 10-13-2016, 05:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-13T02:08:23-07:00","id":986641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/986226-is-cruac-really-this-bad?p=986640#post986640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would tend to agree for the most part...but I'll say this: I just played a game where Touch of the Morrigan came up, and <i>goddamn </i>that is a scary spell in the new system. Our Nosferatu almost got torped in one shot.</div> </div> </div> </